---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { COMPANY } from "../../data/company";
const today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Cliffco Mortgage Bankers" description={`Privacy Policy for ${COMPANY.brandName} (NMLS #${COMPANY.nmls}). Learn how we collect, use, and protect your personal information.`} noindex={false}>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Legal", href: "/legal/" },
    { name: "Privacy Policy", href: "/legal/privacy/" },
  ]} />

  <section class="container-prose pt-12 pb-16">
    <h1 style="font-size: var(--text-display-lg);">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-2">Last updated: {today}</p>

    <p class="mt-6">
      Welcome to cliffcomortgage.com. This site is owned and operated by {COMPANY.legalName}
      (NMLS #{COMPANY.nmls}), operating in Florida as Swish Capital, Inc.
      (collectively, "Cliffco," "we," "us," "our"). Cliffco understands and respects the
      importance of your privacy, and we are committed to protecting it. This Privacy Policy
      describes our practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of information that
      you may provide via this site. Please read this entire Privacy Policy before using or
      submitting information to this site. This site is intended for use by residents of the
      United States.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Sites Covered by This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy applies to the cliffcomortgage.com website. It does not apply to any
      linked sites. To learn about the privacy policy of a linked site, please refer to the
      privacy statement for that site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Visiting Our Website</h2>
    <p>
      You can browse our website without telling us any personal information. You may also be
      able to set your browser to reject cookies, though doing so may limit certain website
      functionality. There are times when you may choose to provide personal information, such
      as requesting that a Cliffco representative call you or requesting a mortgage quote from
      one of our licensed mortgage loan originators. This website does not collect or retain
      your information for any company use except to facilitate contact with you when you
      submit an inquiry or request to speak with us.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Your Consent</h2>
    <p>
      By using this site, you agree to the terms of this Privacy Policy. Whenever you submit
      information via this site, you consent to the collection, use, and disclosure of that
      information in accordance with this Privacy Policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Information We Collect</h2>

    <p class="mt-4 font-medium">Information you provide directly:</p>
    <p>
      Some areas of this site may ask you to submit personally identifiable information, such as
      your name, address, email address, telephone number, and, if applicable, other identifying
      information specific to your inquiry. This may include information submitted to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Request a call from a Cliffco representative.</li>
      <li>Request a mortgage quote from a licensed loan originator.</li>
      <li>Register for a service on this website (if and when applicable).</li>
      <li>Complete a survey (if and when applicable).</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4">
      When you apply for a loan, we collect additional personal information required for loan
      qualification, including Social Security Number (when required for credit-pull
      authorization), financial information, employment history, and income documentation.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 font-medium">Information collected automatically (passive collection):</p>
    <p>
      As you navigate through this site, certain anonymous information can be passively
      collected using technologies such as Internet protocol (IP) addresses, cookies, Internet
      tags or web beacons, and navigational data (log files, server logs, and clickstream data).
      Your browser automatically transmits to this site information such as the URL of the page
      you came from and the IP address and browser version your computer is using.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      We use and may combine such passively collected anonymous information to provide better
      service to site visitors, customize the site based on your preferences, compile and analyze
      statistics and trends, and otherwise administer and improve the site. Such information is
      not combined with personally identifiable information collected elsewhere on the site unless
      you have consented.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 font-medium">Cookies:</p>
    <p>
      A "cookie" is a bit of information that a website sends to your web browser that helps the
      site remember information about you and your preferences. You may set your browser to notify
      you when a cookie is sent or to refuse cookies altogether, but certain features of this site
      might not work without cookies.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Session cookies</strong> are temporary bits of information used to improve
        navigation and collect aggregate statistical information. They are erased once you exit
        your browser or turn off your computer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Persistent cookies</strong> are more permanent bits of information placed on
        your hard drive. They store information such as previously provided preferences and help
        determine what areas of the website visitors find most valuable. Persistent cookies placed
        by this site may hold personally identifiable information only if you have consented to
        the retention of such information.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 font-medium">Loan Officer Personalization Cookie:</p>
    <p>
      When you visit a licensed loan officer's profile page on this website, we may set a
      first-party cookie named <code>cliffco_lo</code> on your browser. This cookie stores
      the identifier of the loan officer whose page you visited and is used solely to display
      that loan officer's contact information as a convenience feature while you continue
      browsing the site. The cookie expires after 30 days, is not shared with any third party,
      and does not collect, transmit, or track any personal information about you. You may
      delete this cookie at any time through your browser settings without affecting your ability
      to use any part of this site.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      Internet tags (also known as single-pixel GIFs, clear GIFs, or invisible GIFs) are smaller
      than cookies and tell the website server information such as the IP address and browser type
      of the visitor's computer. We do not collect or seek personally identifiable information
      through these tags. Navigational data (log files, server logs, and clickstream data) are
      used for system management, to improve the content of the site, for market research, and to
      communicate information to visitors.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 font-medium">Information from third parties:</p>
    <p>
      We may receive information about you from third parties such as credit bureaus, employers,
      asset verifiers, consumer data resellers, and government entities that provide public records.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This website uses Google Analytics to track visitor interactions. Google Analytics uses
      first-party cookies to store information such as the time of the current visit, whether
      you have visited the site before, and the referring website. Google Analytics collects
      the IP address of visitors for geolocation purposes; however, Google Analytics does not
      report actual IP address information to customers. Website owners may also use IP masking
      to instruct Google Analytics to use only a portion of the IP address for geolocation.
      For more information, refer to Google's privacy statements at www.google.com.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>
      Cliffco uses the personal information we collect for the purpose disclosed at the time of
      collection, which may include, but is not limited to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Answering your inquiry and responding to requests for a call or mortgage quote.</li>
      <li>Processing a loan application and originating, underwriting, and servicing mortgages.</li>
      <li>Discussing our products or services with a licensed mortgage loan originator.</li>
      <li>Complying with federal and state mortgage regulations and reporting requirements.</li>
      <li>Analyzing how visitors access and use our site with voluntarily submitted information.</li>
      <li>Sending you marketing about Cliffco's products and services where you have opted in.</li>
      <li>Preventing fraud, complying with legal obligations, and protecting Cliffco and our customers.</li>
      <li>Addressing security issues or system integrity.</li>
      <li>Supporting everyday business operations such as monitoring, reporting, and accounting.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4">
      We will not use your personal information for any other discernible purpose, unless required
      by law.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Access to Your Information</h2>
    <p>
      You may request access to the personal information that Cliffco holds about you by
      contacting a company representative at our corporate offices during regular business hours,
      Monday through Friday, 9:30 a.m. to 5:30 p.m. EST. If you wish to change personal
      information that is out of date or inaccurate, please contact us and we will take all
      reasonable steps to correct any information that is incomplete, inaccurate, or out of date.
      If you wish to have your personal information deleted, please let us know through written
      correspondence and we will process the deletion from our databases wherever practicable
      and as soon as possible.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Disclosure of Information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal information. We may disclose information collected on this site to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The appropriate individuals within our organization or branch office so that someone can respond to your request or tell you about a product or service we offer.</li>
      <li>A Cliffco licensed mortgage loan originator, to provide you with a loan quotation or other information regarding mortgage loan products.</li>
      <li>Investors, agency entities (Fannie Mae, Freddie Mac, FHA, VA, USDA), settlement service providers (title companies, appraisers, credit bureaus), and service providers acting on our behalf under written contracts requiring confidentiality.</li>
      <li>Third parties as permitted or required by law, including regulators, vendors that provide services to us, and law-enforcement authorities.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Security</h2>
    <p>
      Cliffco endeavors to take all reasonable steps to keep any personal information you
      transmit to our site secured, accurate, up to date, and protected from loss, misuse,
      unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction. Personal information is stored
      in secure files.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      The Internet is recognized, at times, not to be a secure method of transmitting
      information. Accordingly, we cannot accept responsibility for the security of information
      that you send to or receive from us over the Internet, or for any unauthorized access or
      use of that information. No Internet transmission is ever 100 percent secure or
      error-free. You should take special care in deciding what information you send to us via
      email, and it is your responsibility to safeguard your use of passwords, ID numbers, and
      other special access features on this site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Contact Forms: Terms and Conditions</h2>
    <p>
      By inputting an email address and/or telephone number, you affirm that they are yours and
      expressly authorize {COMPANY.legalName}, its employees, and/or agents to communicate with
      you or any joint customer through such channels. You consent to be contacted by phone or
      email even if you have previously indicated a preference of "do not call" or "do not email"
      through any government registry or with Cliffco Mortgage Bankers. You agree that calls
      and/or text messages to the telephone number(s) you have provided may involve the use of an
      automatic dialing system or prerecorded voice that we may occasionally use to deliver
      marketing information. Your mobile carrier's charges may apply. You can revoke your
      agreement to be contacted at any time and are not required to consent as a condition of any
      mortgage loan or receiving services from Cliffco Mortgage Bankers. By clicking "Submit" on
      any contact form, you agree that you are providing an electronic signature for yourself and
      that you are authorized to provide an electronic signature for any joint customer.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">SMS / TCPA</h2>
    <p>
      See our <a href="/legal/sms-consent/">SMS Consent</a> page for the text-message terms,
      consent disclosures, and opt-out instructions required under the Telephone Consumer
      Protection Act (TCPA).
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">State Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Residents of states with comprehensive privacy laws (including California, Virginia,
      Colorado, Connecticut, Utah, Florida, Texas, and Oregon) have specific rights, including
      the right to know, the right to delete, the right to correct, the right to opt out of
      certain processing, and the right to data portability. To exercise any of these rights,
      contact us at <a href="mailto:klovece@cliffcomortgage.com">klovece@cliffcomortgage.com</a>
      (ATTN: Kathleen Lovece) or by mail at the address below. See our
      <a href="/legal/ccpa/">CCPA Disclosure</a> for California-specific details.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
      We only collect the personal information you voluntarily give us. If you do not want to
      provide information via the Internet, you may call Cliffco at
      <a href={`tel:${COMPANY.hq.phoneE164}`}>{COMPANY.hq.phone}</a> during regular business
      hours, Monday through Friday, 9:00 a.m. to 5:30 p.m. EST.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      From time to time, we may send you email about our products and services. If you do not
      wish to receive marketing emails from us, please call us at
      <a href={`tel:${COMPANY.hq.phoneE164}`}>{COMPANY.hq.phone}</a> and your address
      will be removed from our marketing lists.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This website is not directed toward children. We do not knowingly collect or post
      information from children younger than the age of 13. You can learn more about children's
      privacy and the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) at the Federal Trade
      Commission's website at <a href="https://www.ftc.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.ftc.gov</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Links to Other Websites</h2>
    <p>
      This site may contain links or references to other websites. Please be aware that we do
      not control other websites and this Privacy Policy does not apply to those websites. We
      encourage you to read the privacy policy of every website you visit.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      Cliffco reserves the right to change, amend, or modify any aspect of this Privacy Policy
      at any time, as deemed necessary. If this Privacy Policy changes, the revised policy will
      be posted on this page with a revised "Last Updated" date. Any changes are effective as of
      the date they are posted. We encourage you to review this page periodically to stay
      informed of any updates.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions, comments, requests, or concerns related to this Privacy Policy
      or the information practices of this site, or if you would like to opt out of future
      communications, please contact us:
    </p>
    <address class="not-italic mt-4">
      {COMPANY.legalName}<br/>
      {COMPANY.hq.street}<br/>
      {COMPANY.hq.city}, {COMPANY.hq.region} {COMPANY.hq.postalCode}<br/>
      <a href={`tel:${COMPANY.hq.phoneE164}`}>{COMPANY.hq.phone}</a>
    </address>
  </section>
</Layout>
